WEBVTT

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.600
Rudy...

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.900
A list of the dead.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.650
It can't be!

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:43.690
No, Rudy isn't on it,
and neither is his family.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.850
Thank God.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.650
So, he lived through the magical disaster.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.690
He's a tough bastard.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:03.350
I wish it had at least sent Paul
to another world or something.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.810
Do you know Paul?!

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:07.900
Huh?

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.690
--What?
--What is it?

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.060
Dear Rudeus,

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:18.150
Zenith, Lilia, and Aisha are missing.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.690
Norn is in my care.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.350
I don't know where you are now,

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:27.850
but I believe that you'll be
able to make it back here alone,

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:32.060
so I'm going to put off looking for you.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.770
I'm going to the Millis Continent.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:38.520
It's Zenith's homeland.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.310
I'll leave a message
with Lilia's family as well.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.440
Search the north of the Central Continent.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.150
If you find them, send word.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.520
Zenith, Lilia, please do the same.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:58.900
Anyone who knows my family or former
members of The Fangs of the Black Wolf:

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.230
Please help find them.

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:05.060
I'm sure some of you
don't think the best of me.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.100
I won't ask you to forgive me.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.060
Insult me if you want.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.810
I'll lick your boots if you want.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:15.690
My whole fortune's gone,
so I can't offer a reward, but please,

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.230
look for my family.

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:25.100
Write to: Millishion Adventurers' Guild,
Holy Millis Kingdom, Millis Continent.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.150
Party: Buena Villager Search Party.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.980
Clan: Fittoa Domain Search Team.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.690
Paul Greyrat.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.010
Mushoku Tensei: Jobless Reincarnation

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:45.600
Our job is to investigate a mysterious
monster in the Petrified Forest.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.600
We get five scrap-iron pieces for
investigating. Two iron pieces if we slay it.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.270
It's a great deal.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.270
What's the mysterious monster?

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:56.230
We're going to investigate
because we don't know.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.770
Is it strong?

00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.440
It might be.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.190
Great! I can't wait to meet it!

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:06.310
Well, we can probably slay it no problem.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.900
We can say goodbye to
money troubles for a while.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.100
Huh?

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.650
Someone's there.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:39.360
What's the big idea?!

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.900
I told you to back off, brats.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.660
Shut up!                 <i>You</i> back off!

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.700
Can't you tell it's more
than you can handle?

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.910
It is not!

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.240
Excuse me.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.540
It's Dead End!

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.540
Huh? What're you doing here?

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.600
He's the guy from...

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.590
Ahem.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:02.170
We came to investigate a mysterious
monster on a job from the Guild.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.020
You, too, huh?

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.010
You, too?

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.470
Yeah, we're here on a similar job.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:14.850
A triple booking? Damn those
screw-ups at the Guild.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.440
Anyway!

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.940
I won't let you brats
run off with our prize!

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:24.990
Go home and get to bed!

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:25.700
What?!

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.370
Wh-Who'd want your help, anyway?!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.660
Then it's first come, first served.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.250
You won't have an easy
time in here, though.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.380
Damn it. Let's get moving!

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.150
What was that about?

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:45.520
It seems like our jobs overlap.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:46.600
Do we give up?

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.150
Of course not.
It's first come, first served.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:52.270
I see! Let's hurry, then!

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.940
Wait.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:59.060
I'm worried about those children.
We should help them.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:01.730
Hurry! We'll get ahead of them!

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:06.810
If we work together too much,
they might figure out you're a Superd.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:07.900
I don't care.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.810
We'll have a lot of
trouble if word gets out.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.060
Would you have us let them die?!

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.730
I understand.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:23.270
We can tail them and only
help if things get desperate.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:24.350
What?!

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:27.480
I thought I'd get to fight
something strong for once!

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:28.980
Come on!

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.350
They're too careless.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:43.980
Don't they realize they're
surrounded by monsters?

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:46.020
Who knows?

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:52.770
Not yet!

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:53.600
Why not?!

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.020
Things aren't desperate yet!

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:07.060
A-An almond anaconda!

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:07.900
I'm going!

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.770
No, wait a little longer!

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.810
We should make them
really appreciate the rescue.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.150
That will do more to boost our reputation.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:18.560
We'll swoop in at the last second.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.600
If they get hurt a little,
I've got healing magic.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.350
My plan is

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:24.900
perfect.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.660
Are you all right?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.740
Y-Yeah.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.460
You saved us.                You guys are tough.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.440
Why did you stop me?

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.150
I could have saved him.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.060
I thought it would work out better for us.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.940
You let a child die just for that?

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.020
Be serious!

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:01.540
I'm thinking as hard as I can, so...

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.920
H-Hey! Don't fight each other.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:08.550
It's our fault that our buddy died.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:13.010
Children can't be blamed.       This is our problem.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.640
We're not kids! We're adventurers!

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:25.310
Your comrade is dead.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.900
I can see that!

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:30.820
But we knew that we could die!

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.990
All adventurers do!

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.700
I'm grateful to you for saving us,

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:42.870
but it's our problem.
No, I couldn't tell how hard the job was.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:46.250
It's... my fault.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.020
Your name is Kurt?

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:14.400
I'm sorry I treated you like a child.
You are full-fledged warrior.

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:33.710
See you. Thanks for bringing us this far.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.260
See you.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:42.020
Good luck!

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:00.100
They're fighting.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.560
Yes.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:28.770
A redhood cobra. I never expected
to find one in this forest.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:31.600
Meaning that's our mysterious monster?

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.980
It seems so.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:37.030
D-Damn it!

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:41.520
That monster is powerful.
I doubt they stood a chance.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:45.520
He'll die if we don't help soon!

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.440
What will we do?!

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:48.600
Can we win?

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:50.440
Definitely.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.190
This time, let's save him!

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:25.940
Again.

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:34.980
Eris!

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:42.150
Now!

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:43.850
R-Right!

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:08.730
We won?

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:15.560
Yes!

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:19.190
We did it! We did it!

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.190
We did, didn't we?

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:23.650
Thank you very much, Ruije--

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:25.230
We were too late.

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:27.020
Huh?

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.370
Hey there, Dead End!

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:51.540
Looks like you've got a lot of baggage.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.880
We just happened to get lucky today.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:00.500
Hey now, what's the rush?

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.050
Is it any of your business?

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.390
You wanna see Jalil
and Vizquel that badly?

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:17.190
Clever trick you pulled, trading jobs.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:20.360
We're done for. How did it come to this?

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:24.240
If I let the Guild know what you've done,

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:28.320
ya'll will lose your licenses.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:30.700
What do you want?

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.790
Oh?     Come on. You know.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.420
I want money. Money.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:40.750
Bring me half of what
you make every month.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.440
Bastard.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:49.520
Why has everything I've done
since I got to this city gone wrong?

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:53.730
Should we pay him now,
then look for a chance to escape?

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.150
No, bad idea.

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:57.400
Even if we make it to the next city,

00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:01.730
we won't be able to earn
a living if they revoke our licenses.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:05.650
Could we put all the blame an
Jalil and Vizquel and play dumb?

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:08.230
No, that ship's sailed.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:11.810
Isn't there some other way?

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:15.440
Ugh. Just thinking about it is a pain.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:17.520
Rudeus?

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:24.980
Don't worry. Leave this to me.

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:32.440
I have to bring this girl--
Eris--back to her home.

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:37.440
To make that happen,
I'd wipe this whole city off the map.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:53.600
Even if it would mean betraying Ruijerd!

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:11.930
D-De-Dea...

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:15.890
Dead End!

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.730
What the...?

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:40.290
Don't kill him, Ruijerd!

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:46.340
I'm sorry.      I-I had no clue you were the real deal.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:50.760
Please. I-I've got kids.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:58.640
We're leaving this city,
so forget about us.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:05.770
But if we get to the next city and
find our licenses have been revoked...

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:15.820
Don't think you can escape me.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.260
Dead End!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.510
Halt!

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:34.770
Ruijerd!

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:54.030
Why are you scared?    He saved your lives, didn't he?

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:58.490
W-Well...                Sorry.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.190
Ruijerd!

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:24.770
Ruijerd! Where are you?!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.150
Come on, Ruijerd!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.690
Oh!

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:50.600
Why don't you say something?

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:52.440
Sorry.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.690
Why are you apologizing?

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:57.810
I should be apologizing to you.

00:17:57.810 --> 00:18:01.270
I was focused on making money efficiently

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:04.900
and improving your reputation
if we got a chance.

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:09.400
And because of my childish schemes...

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:14.230
No. I'm sure you're doing all you can.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:16.650
I'm to blame.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:21.270
I didn't realize how much
you were worrying about.

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:25.150
But earlier, I finally understood.

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:31.690
Just then, when you were ready
to kill him, I sensed your resolve.

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:43.060
You were just desperate
to protect something.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:48.730
Huh?

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:54.020
Having something to
protect makes you a warrior.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:56.100
I'm sorry.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:02.980
What does it mean to be
a warrior to you, Ruijerd?

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:08.150
Being a warrior is my pride.

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:12.690
Warriors protect children
and treasure their comrades.

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.520
I am a warrior.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:20.350
Even if you can't restore my
good name, I will protect you.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:23.350
So, don't worry about the Superd.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:27.020
Just focus on what you protect.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:29.480
Pride...

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:34.060
I will. Thank you.

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:39.270
But I will restore your
reputation, no matter what.

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.730
You never learn.

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:44.310
Do I seem so untrustworthy to you?

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:48.850
I do trust you.
That's why I want to repay you.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.270
You're certainly stubborn.

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:54.440
Not as stubborn as you are.

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:07.020
Well then.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:10.900
Yes.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:19.770
I'm no warrior. Nothing that impressive.

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:19.350
Whoa!

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:22.270
What?! Are you leaving me out?!

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:25.350
To be honest, I don't really understand
what Ruijerd means by "pride."

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:25.190
No, of course not.

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:26.350
Join in, Eris.

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:27.810
But for some reason,

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:29.020
Look out for me from now on.

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:35.350
Ruijerd's approval made me really happy.

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:31.270
I should be asking you that.

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:35.350
I guess I've got no choice!
I'll look out for you!

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.850
Wh-What happened to your head?

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:56.100
I shaved it.

00:20:56.100 --> 00:21:02.100
What happened back there taught me
how much my hair frightens people.

00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:02.850
I see.

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:04.560
Oh, you look good like that!

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:05.810
Seriously?

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.600
Oh, I know!

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.770
I'm sure it was...

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:12.350
Found it!

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:19.270
In that case, we can
hide your third eye, too.

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:22.060
Hey, look!

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:24.100
We all match!

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:27.600
Yes.

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:33.650
Until now, I've been desperate
to figure out everything on my own.

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:38.020
I think that's why I failed this time.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:41.650
We'll run into all sorts
of problems down the road.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:46.940
But when that happens, I'd like us to
all talk it over and decide what to do

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:50.560
so that we won't fight
even if we disagree.

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:51.770
Good.

00:21:51.770 --> 00:21:53.190
Let's do it!

00:21:53.190 --> 00:21:59.270
All right, then, I'd like to begin
the first Dead End strategy meeting.

00:21:59.270 --> 00:22:00.650
Our goal is

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:02.850
the Asura Kingdom!

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.550
Episode 11

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.550
Children and Warriors

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:47.030
Thank you for watching!

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:47.030
Look forward to season two!
